Count REP string iterations as steps

Each iteration of a REP string instruction counts as a step and in
cpu->cycle. When the steps run out with iterations left, the instruction
stops with its registers updated so far and runs again at the next step.
The x86 sandbox relies on this for its instruction budget.

Submitted upstream as https://github.com/hchunhui/tiny386/pull/64 (commit
ff72f7f1358d on tophyr/tiny386 rep-steps).

